body:
Restart required to retarget the template library: `kalide start` captures the deck's configured `templates:` value from `kalide.yaml` at startup (the path exactly as written, resolved as in external-template-library) and pins the resolved library root to it for the life of that session. If the configured `templates:` value changes while the server is running — to a different path, or by adding or removing the key — kalide does NOT retarget live and does NOT fall back to a local `templates/`: it stops serving the deck and serves the standard kalide full-page error telling the user to restart `kalide start` (every served page shows that error, per never-serve-broken-deck). The server keeps running — this is a normal error page, not a crash — so the user can fix `kalide.yaml` and/or restart. Normal serving resumes only after restarting `kalide start`, or when the value is edited back to the one captured at startup. This applies only to a change of the configured `templates:` value: edits of files anywhere under the resolved library root (library.yaml, templates, themes, media) keep live-reloading exactly as before (templates-live-reload), and every other `kalide.yaml` change (title, author, date, theme, navigation, properties) and changes to slides/ and assets/ keep live-reloading as before (live-reload). The comparison baseline is the configured `templates:` value captured at startup (equivalently, the resolved library root).

AC:
- start with `templates: ../shared-lib`, then edit `kalide.yaml` to `templates: ../other-lib` while `kalide start` runs: the next served page is the full-page error telling the user to restart `kalide start`, and no deck is served;
- adding or removing the `templates:` key mid-session yields the same restart-required full-page error, never a silent switch to or from a local `templates/`;
- editing the value back to the startup value (`../shared-lib`) resumes normal serving of the deck without restarting;
- restarting `kalide start` after the retarget serves the deck from the new root (`../other-lib`);
- with the configured value unchanged, editing a file under the resolved library root (e.g. a template layout) still live-reloads, and editing any other `kalide.yaml` key still live-reloads — the restart requirement does not apply to them;
- the error is the standard kalide full-page error and the process keeps running (the listening port stays bound); it is neither a crash nor a partially rendered deck.
